.TH ZOVELIS-WELCOME 1 "October 2026" "Zovelis OS 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zovelis-welcome \- welcome guide and first-run setup for Zovelis OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zovelis-welcome
.RB [ \-\-autostart ]
.RB [ \-\-live | \-\-installed ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zovelis-welcome
greets new users after installation. It lets them choose a light or dark
appearance and a comfortable text size, shows whether the firewall,
automatic security updates and app sandboxing are switched on, and points
to popular applications in the Software Center.
.PP
On the live system (started from a USB stick or DVD) it offers to install
Zovelis OS or to keep trying it.
.PP
The program runs without privileges. Turning automatic security updates on
or off asks for an administrator password (through
.BR pkexec (1))
and runs
.IR /usr/libexec/zovelis/zovelis-admin-helper .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-autostart
Used when started at login: exit quietly if the user chose not to see the
guide at every login.
.TP
.B \-\-live
Show the live-system page even on an installed system.
.TP
.B \-\-installed
Show the installed-system pages even on the live system.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Do not change anything; record the commands that would run.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show all options, including those used by the test-suite.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/zovelis-welcomerc
Whether the guide is shown at every login
.RB ( ShowAtLogin ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemsettings (1),
.BR plasma-discover (1)
